# AGENT.md — src/core/

Business rules. Zero framework dependencies. Zero imports from `adapters/`.

## What lives here

- `entities/` — domain entities. Pure objects that represent business
  concepts. They carry data and any domain invariants.
- `ports/` — abstract interfaces (contracts) the core needs. Typically a
  repository port: `save`, `findAll`, `findById`. The core declares what it
  needs; adapters provide the implementation.
- `use-cases/<module>/` — application-specific business rules. One class per
  operation (e.g. `CreateProductUseCase`, `GetProductsUseCase`). Each use-case
  receives its repository through its constructor.

## Rules

- **Never import Express.** No `Request`, `Response`, `NextFunction`.
- **Never depend on an adapter.** If a use-case needs data, it declares a
  port in `ports/` and receives the implementation at construction time.
- Entities are plain TypeScript classes — no ORM decorators, no persistence
  annotations.
- Use-case tests go next to the use-case (`create-product.use-case.spec.ts`)
  so they are easy to find.
